    "groundingSupports": [
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 36,
       "endIndex": 156,
       "text": "For a standard **Google L6 PM (Staff / Group PM)**, this is an **above-average to strong offer**, particularly on equity"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       0,
       1
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 160,
       "endIndex": 329,
       "text": "However, because you are currently a **Meta IC6 PM (Principal PM)**, happy where you are, and motivated heavily by compensation, **you should not accept this offer as is"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       2,
       3
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 337,
       "endIndex": 445,
       "text": "**The Leveling Mismatch:** Meta IC6 generally maps closer to **Google L7 (Senior Staff / Group PM)** than L6"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       2,
       1,
       3
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 447,
       "endIndex": 523,
       "text": "Google L6 often corresponds to Meta IC5 (or a high-IC5 / low-IC6 borderline)"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       3
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 858,
       "endIndex": 967,
       "text": "Google\u2019s offer letter annualized number ($552,000/year on average) obscures how Google actually pays equity"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       0
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 969,
       "endIndex": 1084,
       "text": "Google typically uses a **front-loaded vesting schedule** (commonly 38% / 32% / 20% / 10% or 33% / 33% / 22% / 12%)"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       0,
       4
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 1087,
       "endIndex": 1143,
       "text": "Assuming the standard **38% / 32% / 20% / 10%** schedule"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       0,
       4
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 1636,
       "endIndex": 1736,
       "text": "Google refresh grants vest over several years and are meant to soften the Year 3 and Year 4 drop-off"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       0
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 1741,
       "endIndex": 1907,
       "text": "Meta\u2019s equity, by contrast, vests evenly at **25% per year** with quarterly vesting, and Meta\u2019s refresher culture for IC6 is among the most aggressive in Big Tech"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       2,
       3
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 1912,
       "endIndex": 2032,
       "text": "At Google, relying on refreshes to prevent a compensation drop in Year 3/4 introduces performance and macroeconomic risk"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       0
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 2129,
       "endIndex": 2160,
       "text": "**Base:** $210,000 \u2013 $250,000"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       0
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 2165,
       "endIndex": 2179,
       "text": "**Bonus:** 20%"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       0
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 2184,
       "endIndex": 2233,
       "text": "**Equity (Annualized):** $180,000 \u2013 $260,000/yr"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       0,
       3
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 2238,
       "endIndex": 2286,
       "text": "**Median Total Comp:** ~$510,000 \u2013 $540,000/yr"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       0,
       4
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 2412,
       "endIndex": 2575,
       "text": "Meta IC6 total comp frequently spans **$580,000 to $800,000+** per year (combining higher base, strong performance multipliers, and larger recurring equity grants)"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       2,
       5,
       3
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 2612,
       "endIndex": 2672,
       "text": "Median L7 total comp sits between **$720,000 and $850,000+**"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       0,
       4,
       3
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 2724,
       "endIndex": 2952,
       "text": "**Sign-On Bonus:** It is standard for Google to offer a **$50,000 \u2013 $100,000+** signing bonus for L6 candidates coming from peer Tier-1 companies (especially Meta), specifically to offset unvested stock and bridge compensation"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       0
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 3061,
       "endIndex": 3153,
       "text": "**Level Alignment:** An IC6 candidate entering as L6 represents a down-level in career scope"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       2,
       1,
       3
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 3208,
       "endIndex": 3283,
       "text": "Since you are content at Meta, you can negotiate from an anchor of strength"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       2
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 3334,
       "endIndex": 3420,
       "text": "Politely raise the scope difference between Meta IC6 (Principal) and Google L6 (Staff)"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       2,
       1
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 3672,
       "endIndex": 3778,
       "text": "If Google is set on L6, require top-of-band compensation and a sign-on bonus to make the switch compelling"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       0
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 4970,
       "endIndex": 5089,
       "text": "**If they meet your counter or offer L7:** Consider accepting if you want a change in product domain or company culture"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       0
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 5198,
       "endIndex": 5336,
       "text": "** Staying at Meta as an IC6 will yield higher comp stability and clearer progression than entering Google at L6 on an unoptimized package"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       2,
       3
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
